{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310720,"nonce":"D7lnIiMMN95Cz7Zv6cYAjDmh7nc=","title":"OPEN — `s.substring(6)` returns the WRONG HALF (\\\"Hello,\\\" of \\\"Hello,World\\\") because the optional end defaults to 0 and Haxe's swap rule ...","message":"**REPRO** (`/tmp/probe/S2.hx`), `var s = \"Hello,World\"`:\n\n| call | got | want |\n|---|---|---|\n| `s.substring(6)` | `Hello,` | `World` |\n| `s.substring(0,5)` | `Hello` | ok |\n| `s.substring(6,11)` | `World` | ok |\n| `s.substr(6)` | `World` | ok |\n\n**MECHANISM.** MIR shows `substring(6)` lowering to\n`haxe_string_substring_ptr(s, 6, 0)` — a literal `0` for the missing end.\nHaxe's rule that a start past the end SWAPS the pair then makes it\n`substring(0, 6)`. The runtime cannot tell that 0 from an explicit\n`substring(x, 0)`, so it cannot be fixed there.\n\n**NOT a general optional-argument bug.** Probed alongside: `indexOf(l)` = 2,\n`indexOf(l,4)` = 9, `substr(6)` = \"World\", `slice(1)`, `sort`, `indexOf` on\narrays — all correct. Optional Int params default to 0, which is the RIGHT\ndefault for indexOf and tolerable for substr (its runtime reads a 0 length as\n\"to the end\"); `substring` is the one where the correct default is the string\nLENGTH.\n\n**FIXED 2026-09-10 in 493c2c20.** THE IDIOM: this codebase declares ONE\nMAPPING PER ARITY, each with its own MIR wrapper — `String_indexOf`\n(params: 1) and `String_indexOf_2` (params: 2) are the model. Added\n`String_substring_1` (params: 1) beside the existing `String_substring`;\nthe 1-arg wrapper calls `haxe_string_length` for its end. Found the idiom by\nnoticing `String_indexOf_2` in a `--stage hir` function listing.\n\nTRAP: adding a mapping row fails `stdlib::runtime_mapping::tests::\nmapping_snapshot_unchanged`. Re-record with\n`RAYZOR_WRITE_MAPPING_SNAPSHOT=1 cargo test -p compiler --lib\nmapping_snapshot_unchanged`, then CHECK THE DIFF is only your row.\n\n**ATTEMPT REVERTED (2026-09-10).** Injecting the length in\n`stdlib_runtime.rs` where `runtime_func == \"haxe_string_substring_ptr\" \u0026\u0026\nargs.len() == 1` was INERT: by that point the HIR call already carries two\narguments, so the defaulting happens further upstream. **Find where an\noptional parameter's default is filled (TAST or HIR, not the mapping) — that\nis the only place the arity is still visible.** `map_method!` declares\n`params: 2` and the mapping layer never pads, so the fill is not there.\n\n`String_substring` (compiler/src/stdlib/string.rs) is a MIR wrapper that only\nforwards; the observed call goes DIRECT to `haxe_string_substring_ptr`, so\nediting the wrapper would not be reached either.\n\nRelated: [[project_haxe_conformance_baseline]].\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_substring_one_arg_defaults_end_to_zero` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}